## 27. README validation before finishing

After creating or updating `README.md`, validate against the
repository.

**Structure:** required sections in order; concise; landing page, not
a specification.

**Accuracy:** stack matches `package.json`; architecture matches
code/docs; schema and relationships match migrations; tree matches the
repo; Git matches `docs/git/branching.md`; Actions match YAML (triggers
and dependencies not invented); install commands and npm scripts exist;
env names match `.env.example`; testing tools match the repo; security
claims are supported.

**Links:** every link exists; relative; no invented paths.

**Status hygiene:** no current branch/PR/SHA/CI/test counts/coverage;
no release banners; no temporary notes.

**AI/agent accuracy:** prompt/skill-driven; human gates preserved;
skills do not auto-run; agent does not merge `main`; production schema
workflow described accurately.

## 28. Final principle

The root `README.md` is a stable public overview of the BankCRM
engineering approach.

```
BankCRM
   ↓
Banking CRM practice / portfolio project
   ↓
Actual features
   ↓
Actual architecture + Supabase/PostgreSQL schema
   ↓
QA + testing + security
   ↓
Git + GitHub + CI/CD
   ↓
AI-assisted SDLC
   ↓
Human decision gates
   ↓
Links to detailed documentation
```

Answer the most important questions for a first-time reader without
duplicating detailed documentation.

**Accuracy is more important than completeness.** If information is
not verifiable from the repository, do not invent it.
